{"id":"8790321df936a708","group":"58","path":"58/batch08/58-df-reductive-group.md","title":"Reductive Group","display":"df-reductive-group — Reductive Group","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-reductive-group","aliases":["58-df-reductive-group","Reductive Group"],"display":"df-reductive-group — Reductive Group","depends_on":["[[../batch01/58-df-algebraic-group.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-reductive-group"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-reductive-group</span><span>Reductive Group</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-reductive-group — Reductive Group"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"07ee726a6e15b274\" href=\"?note=07ee726a6e15b274\" title=\"../batch01/58-df-algebraic-group.md\">../batch01/58-df-algebraic-group.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"k,G,m,i,e,R\\in V\">\\(k,G,m,i,e,R\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{AlgGroup}_k\\subseteq V^4\">\\(\\mathrm{AlgGroup}_k\\subseteq V^4\\)</span> (algebraic-group predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"07ee726a6e15b274\" href=\"?note=07ee726a6e15b274\" title=\"../batch01/58-df-algebraic-group.md\">../batch01/58-df-algebraic-group.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{TrivialUnipotentRadicalData}_S\\subseteq V^6\">\\(\\mathrm{TrivialUnipotentRadicalData}_S\\subseteq V^6\\)</span> (radical-triviality data predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}reductive\\text{-}group}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{TrivialUnipotentRadicalData}_S(G,m,i,e,R,k)\n\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{AlgGroup}_k(G,m,i,e)\\land R=\\{e\\}.\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}reductive\\text{-}group}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{TrivialUnipotentRadicalData}_S(G,m,i,e,R,k)\n\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{AlgGroup}_k(G,m,i,e)\\land R=\\{e\\}.\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>This atom only verifies that a supplied radical candidate is trivial.</li>\n<li>A canonical reductive-group predicate additionally needs an upstream atom certifying that <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"R\">\\(R\\)</span> is the connected normal unipotent radical of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"G\">\\(G\\)</span>; no such atom is currently available in the book.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Humphreys, Linear Algebraic Groups</li>\n<li>Borel, Linear Algebraic Groups</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch01/58-df-algebraic-group.md","status":"resolved","id":"07ee726a6e15b274","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch01/58-df-algebraic-group.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch01/58-df-algebraic-group.md","status":"resolved","id":"07ee726a6e15b274","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{AlgGroup}_k\\subseteq V^4$ (algebraic-group predicate, see [[../batch01/58-df-algebraic-group.md]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"k,G,m,i,e,R\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{AlgGroup}_k\\subseteq V^4","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{TrivialUnipotentRadicalData}_S\\subseteq V^6","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}reductive\\text{-}group}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{TrivialUnipotentRadicalData}_S(G,m,i,e,R,k)\n\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{AlgGroup}_k(G,m,i,e)\\land R=\\{e\\}.","display":true},{"tex":"R","display":false},{"tex":"G","display":false}],"bytes":1122,"backlinks":[{"id":"c13504d25a0786f0","anchor":"ref-5","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$G,m,i,e,R\\in V$ and $\\mathrm{TrivialUnipotentRadicalData}_S(G,m,i,e,R,\\mathbb Q)$ (supplied reductive-group data, see [[58-df-reductive-group]])"},{"id":"81fa5faf3598651a","anchor":"ref-3","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\operatorname{Reductive}$ (reductive-group predicate, see [[../batch08/58-df-reductive-group.md]])"},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-1056","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch08/58-df-reductive-group.md|58-df-reductive-group]]（batch08）"}],"outgoing":["07ee726a6e15b274"]}